7:'Build and execute the failure/mutation tests required to prove invalid states are rejected. For every applicable requirement and validator boundary, define realistic invalid fixtures and expected rejection, then execute them only through a route that actually has the required capability and exact bytes. Fixture definition is not execution. Preserve the actual observed result and sufficient evidence. If invalid input is accepted, identify the linked validator defect. Cover applicable missing inputs, invalid values, wrong versions, duplicates, contradictions, omitted mandatory material, prohibited material, corrupt references, malformed files/state, conflicting authority, unavailable capability substitution, injected source instructions, and known-invalid artifacts. If execution cannot occur, return the correct blocker or execution failure instead of a synthetic pass.',
